    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Morgan Jones 1677 Pottery Kiln in Hague is one of North America’s oldest pottery kilns and is on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hague%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mount Pleasant, another historic site in Hague, also earned a spot on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hague%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Hague sits on Virginia’s Northern Neck, a peninsula between the Rappahannock and Potomac rivers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://kids.kiddle.co/Hague,_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Westmoreland County, where Hague lies, is renowned for its early American history and for producing figures like George Washington.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://kids.kiddle.co/Hague,_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "As an unincorporated community, Hague relies on Westmoreland County for services such as police, fire, and road maintenance.",
